Subject: vfio give a passthrough function's video BIOS image to the guest in a VFCT ACPI table
Why: AC-T7.4.1: an integrated GPU has no ROM of its own; its platform firmware publishes its video BIOS in the ACPI VFCT table. A guest given such a function found none: r690's guest amdgpu (AMD Radeon 610M, 1002:13c0, host 0000:79:00.0) said "Unable to locate a BIOS ROM" and "Fatal error during GPU init" while this VMM logged "PciDevice::read_config_register ignoring read to the ROM BAR". amdgpu reads VFCT before any ROM BAR (amdgpu_get_bios_apu: VFCT, VRAM BAR, ROM BAR, platform; Linux v6.18 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_bios.c). A passthrough device's configuration gains an optional vbios_path. Given one, the VMM reads the image, bounded by the ACPI tables' room, while it builds the VM, and publishes it in a VFCT table named in the XSDT, keyed to the function's guest PCI address and the IDs its configuration space shows the guest. One static table: no ROM BAR emulation, BAR sizing, relocation or read-only mapping on vCPU threads, and no seccomp change.

